  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>Dar es Salaam, Tanzania: <a href=\"/tag/max+healthcare\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Max Healthcare</a> has expanded its foothold in Africa with the launch of its <a href=\"/tag/patient+assistance+centre\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">patient assistance centre</a> (PAC) in Dar es Salaam, Tanzania.This marks the fourth office of the Indian healthcare major in the continent after Nairobi, Addis Ababa &amp; Lagos.According to Max, the new PAC will serve as a local point of engagement for patients in Tanzania and the wider East African region seeking access to advanced tertiary and quaternary healthcare in India.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The centre will connect patients with clinicians through video consults in India and also provide support related to visa/travel assistance, and interpreter services, among other things, the hospital chain added.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>At present, Max Healthcare operates 11 International Offices/PACs operational in different parts of Asia and Africa and receives over 45,000 patients from over 180 nationalities every year.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                  